row.cell:
Hál wes thu, folde,
fira modor;
beo thu growende,
on Codes fæthme;
fodre gefylled,
firum to nytte.

Soil I salute thee,
mother of souls;
be thou growing
by God’s grace;
filled with fodder
folks to comfort.

Yew is outwardly
unpolished tree;
hard and ground-fast,
guardian of fire;
with roots underwattled
the home of the Want.140
